---
/**
 * Privacy policy for justaweb.agency (served at /privacy).
 *
 * WHY: the site runs Google Analytics and Google Ads tags, collects contact-form data,
 * hosts private client tools, and JustAWeb reaches out to businesses using public
 * listing data. Visitors and prospects deserve a plain statement of what is collected
 * and how to opt out, and outbound email needs a policy to point to.
 *
 * HOW: plain language, only claims that match how the site actually works today
 * (Netlify hosting and Forms, GA4 G-K58RVS4CZQ, Google Ads AW-611239252, intake and
 * contract tools in public/, the webgen-pipeline outreach machine and its suppression
 * list). If any of those change, update this page and bump UPDATED. No em dashes.
 * Blake should review it; it is not a substitute for legal advice.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "../data/site.js";

const UPDATED = "September 25, 2026";
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT.email}`;
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | JustAWeb"
  description="How JustAWeb collects, uses and protects information from website visitors, clients and the businesses we contact."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="section">
    <article class="wrap legal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

      <p class="lede">
        JustAWeb is a small web design business run by Blake Goble. This page explains, in plain
        language, what information we collect, why, and the choices you have. We do not sell
        personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        "JustAWeb", "we" and "us" mean JustAWeb (justaweb.agency). Questions or requests about
        your information go to <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you give us</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> Your name, email address and message, plus anything optional you add (business name, current website, timeline). We use it to reply to you and to discuss your project.</li>
        <li><strong>Email.</strong> Anything you send us by email, used the same way.</li>
        <li><strong>Client project tools.</strong> If you become a client, our private project intake form and service agreement collect the business details, content and signature needed to build your site and document our agreement.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments.</strong> Payments are made through services such as Venmo or Zelle. We receive a record that you paid; we never see or store your card or bank details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use this site, such as which pages are viewed and roughly where visits come from. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technology.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising measurement.</strong> We use Google Ads conversion tracking to learn whether our ads lead to contact form submissions. This also uses cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Netlify, processes standard technical data such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested, to deliver and protect the site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Businesses we reach out to</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes we contact a local business that has no website, or an outdated one, to offer
        our services. To do that we use business information that is publicly listed, such as the
        business name, address, phone number, hours, photos and public reviews, which may come
        from map listings through data providers. We may build a sample website from that
        information and share it with the business behind a private, password-protected link.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We contact businesses by email only, and every email says who we are and how to stop hearing from us.</li>
        <li>If you ask us to stop, we add your business to our do-not-contact list and honor it promptly, and we take down any sample site we made for you.</li>
        <li>We never claim to be affiliated with Google or with your business.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to you and provide the services you ask for.</li>
        <li>To build, launch and support client websites.</li>
        <li>To understand and improve this site and our advertising.</li>
        <li>To keep records we are required to keep, such as agreements and payments.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share information only with the service providers that run this site and our
        business, and only for those purposes: Netlify (hosting and form handling), Google
        (analytics and ad measurement) and our email provider. We may also disclose
        information if the law requires it. We do not sell or rent personal information, and we
        do not share it for other companies' marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</li>
        <li>You can opt out of Google Analytics with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
        <li>You can manage ad personalization in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google's ad settings</a>.</li>
        <li>You can ask us to show you, correct or delete the information we hold about you by emailing <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep contact messages and project records for as long as they are useful for your
        project or our business records, and delete them when you ask unless we must keep them
        by law. Our do-not-contact list is kept indefinitely so we can keep honoring it.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reputable providers and limit access to the information we hold. No method of
        storing or sending data online is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable care to
        protect it.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is for businesses and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will update it here and change the date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 760px; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.6rem + 3vw, 3.25rem); }
  .legal__updated { margin-top: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .legal .lede { margin-top: 28px; }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 44px; font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 1.2rem + 0.6vw, 1.625rem); }
  .legal p { margin-top: 14px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .legal ul { margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 1.25em; display: grid; gap: 10px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .legal strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
